# Hash-pinned verification fixtures must check out byte-identical on every
# OS. Without this, Windows checkouts convert LF to CRLF and pinned hashes
# break: the exposure bundle hash chain (proven: CRLF bytes reproduce the
# exact CI error) and the content-addressed execution-map generations
# (generation ID is SHA-256 over complete file bytes; Windows runs
# `bun test scripts`, which loads the map at module scope).
scripts/verification/fixtures/** text eol=lf
docs/PARITY_LEDGER.md text eol=lf
